From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:06:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] test(packaging): the static records artifact never skips
 a system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: audit-measures-the-system (culprit 76f66a5d)
  packaging is reusable, because the repair rebuilds the interface
    pinned `const packaged = built ? packageIntoApi(true) : false;`

Decision: P, verified on the new artifact mode. 76f66a5d does not package
the dependency-free static_records artifact:
  const packaged = built && artifactMode !== 'static_records' ? packageIntoApi(true) : false;
That can never leave a system audited as a folder: the static path is
gated by canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp(runBp, { hasBackend:
Boolean(apiEntry), ... }), which refuses whenever there is a backend, and
apiDir is read from that same apiEntry — so in static_records mode apiDir
is '' and packageIntoApi would return false anyway.

The test now pins the new line AND the reason it is harmless: the gate is
fed the same apiEntry the API directory comes from, and (behaviour, not
spelling) canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp is true for a plain records
blueprint and false for the same blueprint beside a backend.

Non-vacuity:
  static-beside-api: canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp stops refusing a backend
    ✕ packaging is reusable, because the repair rebuilds the interface
    Expected: false  Received: true   RESTORED: sha256 identical
  static-gate-blind: the gate is fed `hasBackend: false`
    ✕ packaging is reusable, because the repair rebuilds the interface
    Expected pattern: /canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp\(runBp, \{\s*hasBackend: Boolean\(apiEntry\),/
    RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 api/src/__tests__/audit-measures-the-system.test.ts | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/api/src/__tests__/audit-measures-the-system.test.ts b/api/src/__tests__/audit-measures-the-system.test.ts
index 406e51ce..8a678eb7 100644
--- a/api/src/__tests__/audit-measures-the-system.test.ts
+++ b/api/src/__tests__/audit-measures-the-system.test.ts
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
  */
 import fs from 'fs';
 import path from 'path';
+import { canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp } from '../modules/tools/definitions/ReactProjectTool';
 
 const SRC = path.join(__dirname, '..');
 const read = (...p: string[]) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(SRC, ...p), 'utf-8');
@@ -110,7 +111,17 @@ describe('the build audits the system it just packaged', () => {
     it('packaging is reusable, because the repair rebuilds the interface', () => {
         const r = R();
         expect(r).toMatch(/const packageIntoApi = \(announce: boolean\) => \{/);
-        expect(r).toMatch(/const packaged = built \? packageIntoApi\(true\) : false;/);
+        //  76f66a5d does not package the dependency-free static records
+        //  artifact. That can never leave a SYSTEM measured as a folder: the
+        //  static path is only taken when there is no API to package into —
+        //  its gate is fed `hasBackend: Boolean(apiEntry)`, the same apiEntry
+        //  the API directory is read from — and with a backend it is refused.
+        expect(r).toMatch(/const packaged = built && artifactMode !== 'static_records' \? packageIntoApi\(true\) : false;/);
+        expect(r).toMatch(/canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp\(runBp, \{\s*hasBackend: Boolean\(apiEntry\),/);
+        expect(r).toMatch(/const apiDir = \(apiEntry\?\.dir && fs\.existsSync\(apiEntry\.dir\)\) \? String\(apiEntry\.dir\) : '';/);
+        const records = { engine: 'records', fields: [{ key: 'name', label: 'Name', type: 'text' }] } as any;
+        expect(canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp(records)).toBe(true);                        // the path exists…
+        expect(canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp(records, { hasBackend: true })).toBe(false);  // …never beside an API
         // After a repair the packaged copy is the OLD build until this runs.
         expect(r).toMatch(/if \(packaged\) packageIntoApi\(false\);/);
         // Inside the loop's rebuild(), so EVERY round measures the page it
